    "palette": "blue-orange",
    "font": "helvetica",
    "step_markers": "circled-numbers",
    "language": "en",
    "version": 2,
    "caption_draft": "Figure 1. Full-stack architecture and end-to-end workflow of colabctl. (1) Both the loopback-secured Web/Chromium UI and CLI drive the shared controller; (2) it acquires the multi-account pool lock and provisions a GPU VM (T4/L4/A100/G4/H100) via the Colab Control API (auto-reaping newly leaked orphans on timeout). (3) Over Jupyter WebSocket, colabctl probes GPU/RAM and deploys a detached watchdog.py daemon, then (4) writes an Included ssh_config and pre-warms one ControlMaster SSH-over-WS tunnel. (5) Concurrent terminals, VS Code Remote-SSH, and -L port forwards share this single slot without HTTP 429, while (6) status/extend/guard use a fast no-PTY mux channel (~1s). (7) Inside the VM, the Cost-Guard Watchdog polls GPU (<5%) and PTY I/O every 15s and fires POST $TBE_RUNTIME_ADDR/unassign on idle (30m) or hard deadline (4h) even when the host is offline; (8) stop tears down the mux, unassigns the VM, and removes the SSH alias.",
    "open_questions": [],
    "notes": "Dashed strokes are reserved strictly for control/monitoring edges; all three region containers use solid frames. Flat linear Lucide icons are embedded inline inside node groups as data-symbol elements."
  },
